As one could expect even without reading the sources of 'R CMD
javareconf', the script is modifying the permissions.

$ R --version
R version 3.2.3 (2015-12-10) -- "Wooden Christmas-Tree"
Copyright (C) 2015 The R Foundation for Statistical Computing
Platform: x86_64-redhat-linux-gnu (64-bit)

# stat /usr/lib64/R/etc/ldpaths
...
Access: (0644/-rw-r--r--)  Uid: (    0/    root)   Gid: (    0/    root)
...

# inotifywait --monitor --timefmt '%s' --format '%w %T %e' \
--outfile what-s_happening /usr/lib64/R/etc/ldpaths & 

# R CMD javareconf

# stat /usr/lib64/R/etc/ldpaths
...
Access: (0600/-rw-------)  Uid: (    0/    root)   Gid: (    0/    root)
...

# cat what-s_happening 
/usr/lib64/R/etc/ldpaths 1461430370 OPEN
/usr/lib64/R/etc/ldpaths 1461430370 ACCESS
